<section>
  <h2>Understanding PDF Passwords</h2>
  <p>PDFs can have two types of passwords:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Owner Password (Permissions Password):</strong> Controls what users can do with the PDF (print, copy, edit, etc.)</li>
    <li><strong>User Password (Open Password):</strong> Required to open the PDF at all</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can remove an owner password if you know it. You cannot remove a user password without knowing it - that would be illegal decryption.</p>
</section>

