<section>
  <h2>Can You Remove a PDF Password You Forgot?</h2>
  <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> No, not legally.</p>
  <p>PDF encryption is strong. If you don't know the user password and the file has one, there's no legitimate way to unlock it. Services that claim to "crack" PDF passwords are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Often malware in disguise</li>
    <li>Illegal in some jurisdictions</li>
    <li>Unreliable and potentially harmful to your computer</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>What to do instead:</strong> Contact the document owner or creator and ask for an unlocked version.</p>
</section>

