<section>
  <h2>How to Avoid Password Problems</h2>

  <h3>1. Use a Password Manager</h3>
  <p>Store all your passwords (including PDF passwords) in a password manager like 1Password, LastPass, or Bitwarden. Never forget a password again.</p>

  <h3>2. Document Your PDFs</h3>
  <p>Keep a simple spreadsheet or note with PDF passwords you create. Update it whenever you create a new protected PDF.</p>

  <h3>3. Use Simple Passwords for Internal Documents</h3>
  <p>If you're just preventing accidental opens within your team, use simple passwords like "Company2024" or "Internal". Don't overcomplicate it.</p>

  <h3>4. Consider Alternative Protection</h3>
  <p>Instead of password protection, consider: watermarking with recipient info, limiting sharing through access controls, or using secure document portals.</p>
</section>

